From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 19 Jan 2026 18:46:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: xenio: split context into shared and per-queue parts

Split td_xenio_ctx into td_xenio_shared_ctx (grant table handle, pool
name, blkifs list) and a per-queue td_xenio_ctx (event channel handle,
port, ring event).

Each queue now owns its own event channel, removing the
xenio_pending_queue() hack that searched across all queues to find which
one an event belonged to. The ring event handler receives the queue
directly, enabling independent event handling per queue.

Every request still share the same lists in tapdisk; and tapdisk
is still mono-thread.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
